rror (cascade):**  \n- Both (10) and (12) are invalid; therefore (14) is baseless.\n\n> \u201cIn a triangle, the external symmedian issued from a vertex divides the opposite side **externally** in the ratio of the adjacent sides (a standard property of symmedians, proved by applying the law of sines \u2026).\u201d\n\n**Issue \u2013 Critical Error:**  \n- The external symmedian divides the opposite side externally in the ratio of the **squares** of the adjacent sides, not the sides themselves.  \n- The statement of the property is incorrect, undermining the subsequent identification of\u202fX\u202fas the external\u2011symmedian foot.\n\n> \u201cTherefore (14) shows that the point\u202fX\u202fis exactly the point where the external symmedian of\u202f\u0394BEF\u202fissued from\u202fB\u202fmeets the line\u202fMN.\\) \u2026 Hence\u202f\u2113\u202fcoincides with the external symmedian of\u202f\u0394BEF\u202fthrough\u202fB.\\)\u201d\n\n**Issue \u2013 Critical Error:**  \n- Because the ratio in (14) is not the correct symmedian ratio, the identification of\u202f\u2113\u202fas the external symmedian is unjustified.\n\n---\n\n### 2.7. External\u2011symmedian\u2013tangency Lemma  \n\n> **Lemma.** \u201cLet\u202f\u0394XYZ\u202fhave circumcircle\u202f(XYZ). The external symmedian through vertex\u202fX\u202fmeets\u202f(XYZ)\u202fagain at a point\u202fT\u2260X. Then the line\u202fXT\u202fis tangent to\u202f(XYZ)\u202fat\u202fT.\u201d\n\n**Issue \u2013 Critical Error:**  \n- This lemma is false. The external symmedian does **not** generally pass through a point of tangency on the circumcircle.  \n- Moreover, the proof given uses the incorrect side\u2011ratio property (adjacent sides rather than their squares) and misapplies the law of sines.  \n- Consequently the lemma cannot be invoked.\n\n---\n\n### 2.8. Final step  \n\n> \u201cFrom (15) the line through\u202fH\u202fparallel to\u202fAP\u202fis the external symmedian of\u202f\u0394BEF\u202fthrough\u202fB. Applying the Lemma \u2026