n circle.\u201d\n\n*Verification:*  \n- The phrase \u201ccentral angles \\(\\angle CPE\\) and \\(\\angle DPF\\)\u201d is meaningless in this context: \\(P\\) is not the centre of \\(\\Omega\\) nor of \\(\\Gamma\\); therefore these are not central angles of those circles.  \n- The inference \u201cSince \\(PC=PD\\), the chords \\(CE\\) and \\(DF\\) have equal length\u201d is **incorrect**; equality of radii from \\(P\\) to \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) does not impose any relation between the lengths \\(CE\\) and \\(DF\\).  \n- Consequently the claim that \\(C,D,E,F\\) are concyclic is unsupported.  \n\n**Classification:** Critical Error \u2013 the entire lemma rests on false statements.\n\n---\n\n### Lemma\u202f4\n> \u201cThe line \\(AB\\) meets the circle \\((C D E F)\\) at the two points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) (they are the second intersections of \\(AB\\) with \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\)). By the power\u2011of\u2011a\u2011point theorem applied to point \\(B\\) we obtain \\(BC\\cdot BD = BE\\cdot BF\\).\u201d\n\n*Verification:*  \n- Points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) lie on the line \\(MN\\), not on the line \\(AB\\). Hence the line \\(AB\\) does **not** intersect the circle \\((C D E F)\\) at \\(C\\) and \\(D\\).  \n- The power\u2011of\u2011a\u2011point relation stated is therefore based on a false intersection configuration and is invalid.  \n\n**Classification:** Critical Error \u2013 the premise of the power\u2011of\u2011a\u2011point application is false.\n\n---\n\n### Lemma\u202f5\n> \u201cFrom Lemma\u202f4 we have \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{BE}{BF}= \\frac{BC}{BD}\\). \u2026 By the intersecting\u2011chords theorem applied to the two original circles we obtain \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{BC}{BD}= \\frac{CM}{DN}\\). Finally Lemma\u202f1 gives \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{CM}{DN}= \\frac{r}{R}\\).\u201d\n\n*Verification:*  \n- The first equality \\(\\frac{BE}{BF}= \\frac{BC}{BD}\\) depends on Lemma\u202f4, which is false.  \n- The \u201cintersecting\u2011chords theorem\u201d claim that \\(\