he solution\u2019s core arguments (similarity of triangles, position of the orthocenter, inversion mapping, ratio computations, identification of a symmedian, the symmedian\u2011tangent lemma, and the orthocentre coincidence) all contain **critical errors**, the final statement that \u201cthe line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\u201d is not proved. The solution is therefore **invalid**."
